      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e these are the public headers. All these annotations make it hard to read and understand the signatures. Are they necessary?\n\nUnfortunately yes. We could make a clean version in a comment just before the declaration. Otherwise we have the reference in README.md or on developers.google.com/speed/webp.\n\n```\nsrc/dec/webp_dec.c:749:17: error: conflicting \u0027__counted_by\u0027 attribute with the previous function declaration\n  749 | int WebPGetInfo(const uint8_t* WEBP_COUNTED_BY(data_size) data,\n      |                 ^\nsrc/webp/decode.h:55:16: note: previous declaration is here\n   55 | WEBP_NODISCARD WEBP_EXTERN int WebPGetInfo(\n      |                ^\nsrc/webp/./types.h:68:21: note: expanded from macro \u0027WEBP_EXTERN\u0027\n   68 | #define WEBP_EXTERN extern __attribute__((visibility(\"default\")))\n```",
      "parentUuid": "69f7d7fb_f585cb06",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 26
